WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.096
This work,

00:00:04.176 --> 00:00:08.271
presented at NeurIPS 2022 by Johan Larsson and
Jonas Wallin of Lund University,

00:00:08.351 --> 00:00:12.447
introduces the Hessian Screening Rule,

00:00:12.527 --> 00:00:16.622
a new way to speed up fitting the lasso
regularization path.

00:00:16.702 --> 00:00:20.798
Screening rules discard predictors before a model
is fit, shrinking the problem.

00:00:20.878 --> 00:00:24.973
The authors show that using second-order Hessian
information yields both far tighter screening

00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:29.149
and much more accurate warm starts,

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:33.324
especially when predictors are highly correlated,
where existing rules struggle most.

00:00:33.404 --> 00:00:37.500
The result is a method that is the fastest across
nearly every simulated and real benchmark they tested.
